guamp: metal2vulkan bridge patch 0024, an _sRGB extended-range blend beyond fast math's model takes the rounded model (AegirPoster)

fin48/fin49: AegirPoster died at every boot on "render pipeline: Unsupported { feature: ExtendedRangeBlend(SrgbForm), needs:
NotImplemented, ... calliope_star_fsh }": QuartzCore's poster shader blends into BGRA10_XR_sRGB (its CAMetalLayer is XR10 since
0018) with a blend fast math's measured model does not hold, and metal2vulkan refused the pipeline. Without fast math every such
blend is built (the output rounded to half first, each term's product and the sum rounded); bridge/patches/0024 takes that model
for these blends instead of the refusal, in Blend::of and in Blend::for_output (a half4 output or a float4 one rounded to half).
The result may differ from Metal's fast arithmetic by those roundings (not measured); the unit expectations of the two refused
cases (tests.rs) now expect no gap. The GPU workflow stacks every bridge/patches/*.patch after the device patches, so the new
file is built. Applies after 0001-0003, 0009-0021 and 0030.

